# This project uses Vite's mode-based env files instead of manual .env
# juggling:
#
#   .env.development   -> loaded automatically by `npm run dev`
#                          (already committed, points at localhost:4000)
#
#   (none for production) -> `npm run build` intentionally has no
#                          VITE_API_URL set. Nginx makes the API
#                          same-origin in production (see
#                          deploy/nginx.conf.example), so the frontend
#                          just calls relative paths like /api/vouches.
#
# You generally shouldn't need a plain `.env` file at all. If you do
# (e.g. testing against a deployed API from your local machine), copy this
# to `.env.local` (gitignored) and set your own value:
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
